SUMMARY:Underwater Exploration
DESCRIPTION:What lives below the surface? Though we can’t always see it\, the pond at Prairie Ridge is teeming with life\, big and small. Join us for the second day of the City Nature Challenge as we look to see how many aquatic species we can find. We will meet at the Chimney Swift tower before walking as a group down at the pond\, about a five-minute walk from the parking lot down the Prairie Trail. Bring water\, whatever camera you have\, and wear shoes you don’t mind getting wet and muddy! This program welcomes ages 8+. \nRegistration is required to attend this program. \nRegister
URL:https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/underwater-exploration/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Children,Citizen Science,K-12 Students,Outdoor Experiences,Teens
