SUMMARY:Birdwatching for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:Want to try birdwatching but aren’t sure how to get started? Join us for a laid-back program where you’ll learn the basics of identifying common birds! We will slowly walk about a mile to look for birds in different areas. We will learn which collaborative science projects we can contribute our birdwatching data to. \nThis program is for both adults and kids age 8+. Please dress for the weather\, wear closed-toed shoes and bring water. It will be helpful to download the free bird apps eBird and Merlin Bird ID. We will meet in front of the building next to the parking lot before walking as a group down the trails. \nRegistration is required to attend this program. \nRegister
URL:https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/birdwatching-for-beginners-7/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Children,Citizen Science,Educators,K-12 Students,Outdoor Experiences,Teens
