SUMMARY:Lifelong Hike: Holly Shelter
DESCRIPTION:Holly Shelter Game Land in Pender County covers over 65\,000 acres in Pender County.  Here we will explore the Longleaf Pine savannas and associated pocosins rich in carnivorous plants and colorful orchids. The carnivorous plant diversity here is worth the visit alone.  We will ride through the game land with several stops and short walks from the bus. \nPlease note: You will be required to enter the following information for each registrant before you can complete your registration: emergency contact\, physician contact and health information (allergies\, conditions\, medications relevant to this field experience). Take a moment to gather this information before beginning your registration. \nREGISTRATION FOR THIS TRIP IS FULL \nIf the trip is full\, please email Missy Chernick to be added to the waitlist. \nRegistration deadline: Monday\, May 4 at 7:00 AM \nFor additional information about this trip and other Lifelong Hikes & Adventures\, contact Jerry Reynolds at 919.707.9884.
URL:https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/lifelong-hike-holly-shelter/
LOCATION:In the Field
CATEGORIES:Adults,Lifelong Learners,Outdoor Experiences,Trips
END:VEVENT
